{'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 7, 10, 11, 0, 32, 704834, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'task_id': '1f71c9a66044', 'workflow_id': '37ade998c6f048a5', 'iteration': 1, 'files': [{'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 7, 10, 11, 0, 32, 704812, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'path': 'fibonacci.py', 'content': 'def fibonacci(n: int) -> int:\n    """\n    Return the n-th Fibonacci number using an iterative approach.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The index of the Fibonacci number to compute (non-negative integer).\n\n    Returns:\n        The n-th Fibonacci number.\n        - fibonacci(0) returns 0\n        - fibonacci(1) returns 1\n        - For n >= 2, returns the sum of the two preceding numbers.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is negative.\n    """\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError("n must be a non-negative integer")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b\n'}], 'explanation': 'Implemented an iterative Fibonacci function with type hints, docstring, and proper error handling for negative inputs. Uses O(1) space and O(n) time complexity.'}